<title>USA: Horizon Cellular sells properties to PriCellular.</title>
<headline>Horizon Cellular sells properties to PriCellular.</headline>
<dateline>MALVERN, Pa. 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Horizon Cellular Group said on Tuesday it agreed to sell some Kentucky cluster properties to PriCellular Corp for $116.5 million of cash and stock.</p>
<p>The sale, which requires regulatory approval, is expected to close before year-end. The four markets, KY-4, 5, 6 and 8 have over 234,000 subscribers and about 756,000 pops.</p>
</text>
